  "reasoning": "The patient presents with three distinct symptoms that collectively point to a single systemic condition. First, frequent yeast infections are a classic clinical indicator of diabetes, as chronically elevated blood glucose levels create an environment that promotes fungal overgrowth. Second, excessive sweating and getting hot easily are commonly associated with autonomic neuropathy or metabolic dysregulation, both of which are well-documented complications of diabetes. Third, trouble breathing during exercise can result from cardiovascular deconditioning, poor circulation, or early microvascular complications frequently seen in diabetic patients. While each symptom could theoretically relate to other conditions individually, their combination strongly establishes diabetes as the unifying diagnosis.",
